{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/356747-2e-speculation-types-of-milestones","id":356747,"title":"[2e Speculation] Types of Milestones","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-01T12:20:16-08:00","id":356747,"title":"[2e Speculation] Types of Milestones","content":"I'm desperate for another spoiler, so I thought I'd stir the pot a little. It seems there will be at least two types of milestones in 2nd edition: universal and superlative.<br /> <br /> Universal milestones, I would wager, are things that all Prometheans can use to propel the Pilgrimage. I'd wager this would be stuff like building a new Promethean, experiencing Torment for the first time, and going to the River of Death. They also can cause Wastelands to form due to an unflux of Pyros, so they're probably worth a fair bit Vitriol.<br /> <br /> Superlative milestones seem to be the most common ones. They're tied to Roles, and also likely the things the Storyteller plans for the Promethean. Big, dramatic moments that the plot turns on.<br /> <br /> I'm willing to bet there's also going to be a third type of milestone that fills in the sort of supernatural Aspirations that Mages and Werewolves have (what wyrdhamster cooked up for a &quot;1.5&quot; game <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/353813-2ed-hack-milestones-as-aspirations\">here</a>). These are things the player wants their character to experience in some way.<br /> <br /> That's about everything I can remember to piece together about milestones. Have I missed anything? Any other ideas about superlative milestones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:11:10-08:00","id":356814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/356747-2e-speculation-types-of-milestones#post356747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm desperate for another spoiler, so I thought I'd stir the pot a little. It seems there will be at least two types of milestones in 2nd edition: universal and superlative.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Superlative milestones seem to be the most common ones. They're tied to Roles, and also likely the things the Storyteller plans for the Promethean. Big, dramatic moments that the plot turns on. </div> </div> </div>Uh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's about everything I can remember to piece together about milestones. Have I missed anything? </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://dl.dropboxusercontent.com/u/4464486/superlative.png\" target=\"_blank\">Hugely.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:43:37-08:00","id":356851,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">That's great that the term comes from 1e, and I'm sure you're right that a lot of that terminology will be making it's way back into the new edition. But how is it going to translate?<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\">Do you think a superlative milestone would give out 9 Vitriol Beats, for instance? The Roles blog post states that a superlative milestone &quot;is always a step forward along his Pilgrimage.&quot;</span></span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Cxuog44JenzbN7GaAyRqDO4DXce9VGv6ybaCv9yYsPk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Simulacre: An Alternative Morality Stat for Prometheans</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/9523-the-alchemy-lab-homebrew-athanors\" target=\"_blank\">Homebrew Athanors</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/887-metamurpho","name":"Metamurpho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar887_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-01T13:56:52-08:00","id":356866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metamurpho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/356747-2e-speculation-types-of-milestones?p=356851#post356851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think a superlative milestone would give out 9 Vitriol Beats, for instance? The Roles blog post states that a superlative milestone &quot;is always a step forward along his Pilgrimage.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak to the particular numbers, but given that (despite Humanity no longer being the Integrity-equivalent in 2e) 1e's section on Humanity ends its bulleted list thusly\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PtC 1e Core p95</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Humanity is used as the dice pool to determine whether a Promethean makes the transition to Mortality at the end of his Pilgrimage. This moment is called the Rebirth, and low Humanity can cause to fail it, <b>even if all the milestones of the Pilgrimage were completed superlatively.</b> (See \u201cAttaining the Lapis Philosophorum : Mortality\u201d on p. 194.)</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026 I think it's a safe bet that superlative milestones remain huge steps on the Pilgrimage, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}